# "Using a rune from the bag"). The purse is the player's store inbox (CONST_SLOT_STORE_INBOX), outside inventory slots
# 1-10, and every walk by item type starts at slots 1-10: a magic rune in the Rune Bag that lies in the purse was never found
# by a hotkey, the action bar or the helper (Game::internalGetThing -> Game::findItemOfType), never counted by
# player:getItemCount / Player::getItemTypeCount and never taken by player:removeItem / Player::removeItemOfType.
# The one rule (new header src/chaosrunebag.h): the items DIRECTLY inside a container of the Rune Bag type that lies DIRECTLY
# in the store inbox. Nothing else of the purse is visited (not a plain item, not a Loot Bag, not a pouch of another kind).
#   * Game::findItemOfType (a player, depthSearch): after slots 1-10 and the bags in them, the Rune Bag in the purse. The
#     hotkey branch of internalGetThing, the action bar, the helper and player:getItemById(id, true) all end here. A rune in
#     the backpack is therefore always preferred; the purse is the last place.
#   * Player::getItemTypeCount, countRemovableItemsOfType (so removeItemOfType, the NPC sell checks and player:getItemCount),
